invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_ifma.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: poly1305_ifma.c drops the target attribute that turns AVX-512F and
  AVX-512 IFMA on for its own functions, so the kernel compiles only where
  the whole object is built with those instructions, and an object built
  that way runs AVX-512 in code the caller's CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA bit never
  chose. The script compiles the native copy for x86-64 with no instruction
  flag, as a host object compiles it, and the compile fails: each
  intrinsic needs a feature that only the attribute turned on.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx512f,avx512ifma"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("avx512f,avx512ifma")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
